{
 "name": "tagged_application_burst",
 "story": "Cloud hosts with no service map between them, related only by the tags on their resources. Four hosts of one application pin their CPU over twelve minutes (an antivirus scan across a farm) and are one incident. A host of another application, and the same application's dev host, alarm in the middle of it and are not part of it. Later, a pool of desktops: one host's disk alarm has fired every half hour for hours, so it is noisy; a second host's disk alarm that starts two minutes after one of its firings joins it, and a third that starts twelve minutes after one does not.",
